# Byte-stable checkouts -- store and restore files exactly as committed.
#
# This repository has no uniform end-of-line convention: README.md and most
# other files are LF, while six run logs are CRLF as Python wrote them on
# Windows.  core.autocrlf (true in the system gitconfig) normalised those
# logs to LF on commit, so a fresh clone with core.autocrlf=false produced
# files whose SHA-256 no longer matched PROVENANCE.txt and CHECKSUM.sha256.
#
# "* -text" disables EOL conversion on both add and checkout: git stores the
# bytes on disk verbatim and restores them verbatim on any platform, so the
# recorded hashes hold for every clone regardless of core.autocrlf.  No file
# content is modified by this setting.
* -text
